  "notes": [
   "Arduino Due, Arduino Motor Shield and wall wart supply are not in the catalogue, so they are new part types; only the ports used are meaningful for the shield (pins 3 PWM_A, 12 DIR_A, 9 BRAKE_A, A0 SNS_A).",
   "The motor's two wires are permanently attached to the motor, so motor ports 1/2 connect straight to the shield's channel A screw terminals (red to +, black to -, as in the photo); no jumper wires are used.",
   "The shield is stacked on the Due so every shield header pin is joined to the matching Due socket; only the pins the sketch uses plus power pins are listed.",
   "Wall wart (12V used with the fan) plugs into the Due DC jack; its mains plug is not modelled. The DC- side is internal to the barrel jack, so only DC+ is wired to DC-JACK.",
   "The USB cable goes to the Due programming port (USB-PROG) and to the computer; the photo shows both USB and power cables attached."
